_text":"Exile the top two cards of your library. Until the end of your next turn, you may play those cards.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-11-13","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"},{"cmc":2.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}{U}","name":"Twincast","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","oracle_text":"Copy target instant or sorcery spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2009-07-17","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Wastes","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2025-08-01","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You must still pay all costs to cast those spells and follow normal casting permissions. For example, if one of the exiled cards is a sorcery, this effect doesn't allow you to cast it during an opponent's turn.","oracle_id":"584cf0fd-112a-4ca6-9c0e-1f3228a7d325","published_at":"2021-11-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell has damage divided as it was cast, the division can't be changed, although the targets receiving that damage still can. The same is true of spells that distribute counters.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell that's copied has an X whose value was determined as it was cast, the copy will have the same value of X.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell that's copied is modal (that is, it says \"Choose one —\" or the like), the copy will have the same mode. A different mode can't be chosen.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The copy is created on the stack, so it's not \"cast.\" Abilities that trigger when a player casts a spell won't trigger. The copy will resolve before the original spell does.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The copy will have the same targets as the spell it's copying unless you choose new ones. You may change any number of the targets, including all of them or none of them. If, for one of the targets, you can't choose a new legal target, then it remains unchanged (even if the current target is illegal).","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Twincast can copy any instant or sorcery spell, not just one with targets.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can't choose to pay any alternative or additional costs for the copy. However, effects based on any alternative or additional costs that were paid for the original spell are copied as though those same costs were paid for the copy.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Because exiling a card with foretell from your hand is a special action, you can do so any time you have priority during your turn, including in response to spells and abilities. Once you announce you're taking the action, no other player can respond by trying to remove the card from your hand.","oracle_id":"99915b5a-5092-4900-8824-6de2aab1b2c1","published_at":"2022-06-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Casting a foretold card from exile follows the timing rules for that card. If you foretell an instant card, you can cast it as soon as the next player's turn. In most cases, if you foretell a card that isn't an instant (or doesn't have flash), you'll have to wait until your next turn to cast it.","oracle_id":"99915b5a-5092-4900-8824-6de2aab1b2c1","published_at":"2022-06-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Delayed Blast Fireball deals 5 damage if it was cast from exile for any reason; it doesn't have to be from its foretell ability.","oracle_id":"99915b5a-5092-4900-8824-6de2aab1b2c1","published_at":"2022-06-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you're casting a foretold card from exile for its foretell cost, you can't choose to cast it for any other alternative costs. You can, however, pay additional costs, such as kicker costs. If the card has any mandatory additional costs, those must be paid to cast the spell.","oracle_id":"99915b5a-5092-4900-8824-6de2aab1b2c1","published_at":"2022-06-10","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
